{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of the neurology team. You were brought in last night because of some tremors in your face and neck. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I was at rehab, doing okay after my last infection. Then yesterday, my face started shaking—couldn’t stop it. Hard to talk. Also felt short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever. But I had chills. And I fell—hit my face. That’s when they sent me here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for letting me know. We’ve checked a CT scan of your head, and there’s no bleeding or stroke. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So… is it a seizure? Or something from the fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but we don’t think it’s a seizure. The tremors might be related to your recent antibiotic—Ciprofloxacin. It can cause this in some patients, especially with other risk factors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… I was on that for my bladder infection. Should I stop it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve already stopped it. You’re now on a different IV antibiotic called Zosyn, which covers both your previous infection and possible pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pneumonia? I didn’t know I had that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows some new changes in the left lung. Given your history of swallowing issues and recent fall, we think you may have aspirated—inhaled something—which led to pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense… I’ve had trouble swallowing before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2177-08-26 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s likely why you became hypoxic—your oxygen was low. We’ve had you on oxygen, and it’s helping. We’ll keep monitoring that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2177-08-26 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted neurology, and they’ve started you on a medication called Clonazepam to help with the tremors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2177-08-26 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2177-08-26 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve reviewed everything. It’s safe. We also lowered your Celexa dose slightly—sometimes that can worsen tremors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2177-08-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are the tremors now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2177-08-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I can talk more clearly. Still a little shaky, but not like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2177-08-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re going to do an EEG today to make sure there’s no seizure activity in your brain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2177-08-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "An EEG? Like wires on my head?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2177-08-26 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. It’s painless. Just records your brain waves. Helps us rule out seizures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2177-08-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your EEG results are back. No seizure activity. There’s some mild slowing in one area, but no epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2177-08-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it wasn’t a stroke or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2177-08-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. The tremors were likely a side effect of Ciprofloxacin, possibly worsened by the pneumonia and recent fall. Now that we’ve stopped Cipro and treated the infection, you’re improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2177-08-27 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not something more serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2177-08-27 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. Your oxygen levels are better. We’ve weaned you down to 2 liters, and your lungs are clearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2177-08-27 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll switch you to an oral antibiotic tomorrow—Clindamycin—for another week to finish treating the pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2177-08-27 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I won’t need IV anymore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2177-08-27 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re ready to go back to oral meds. You’re stable enough to return to rehab tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2177-08-27 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I miss my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2177-08-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat chest X-ray looks better. The pneumonia is responding well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2177-08-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tremors are almost gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2177-08-27 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll restart your statin soon—it was held temporarily. Your heart and blood vessel meds are all continuing as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2177-08-27 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also want to make sure you follow up with urology for your kidney mass and bladder issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2177-08-27 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had that checked in a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2177-08-27 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s important. And neurology would like to see you in two months to monitor any movement issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’re going to discharge you back to rehab today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take Clindamycin four times a day for seven days. We’ve stopped Ciprofloxacin. Your other meds are mostly the same, with a few small changes like lower trazodone and continued tolterodine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the tremors come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very unlikely now. But if they do, or if you develop fever, shortness of breath, or swelling, call your doctor or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2177-08-28 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Keep up with your follow-ups, and take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check—your oxygen is 96% on room air, and you’re walking with your walker without trouble."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel strong enough to go back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. The transport team will take you back to rehab in about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll follow all the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send your records to rehab and your doctors. Make sure you keep those follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Especially with urology and neurology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. You’ve made great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2177-08-28 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to hear that. Keep up the good work."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2177-08-26 06:46:00",
